    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d782">

                <pb facs="1255" n="1241" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1241"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 E.W./7–1244: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-12T18:00:00-04:00">July 12, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5472. For Phillips. If proposal outlined in your 5477 July 12 is agreeable to the
                    British, we have no objection to statement being issued by the Supreme Allied
                        Commander.<anchor n="26" xml:id="d782-f1"/> We would regard such a statement
                    as being without prejudice to the proposal for a further statement on a
                    governmental basis should that be considered desirable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <pb facs="1256" n="1242" xml:id="pg1242"/>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[For texts of statements by the Secretary of State issued on July 14, 1944,
                        on Nazi atrocities in Hungary and Greece, see Department of State <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, July 16, 1944, page 59.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d782-f1" n="26" xml:id="d782-f1-content">
                <p>For text of the warning, see the London <hi rendition="#italic">Times</hi>, July
                    17, 1944, p. 3, col. 3.</p>
            </note>
